    "breadcrumb": "Podpora Swing Catalyst \u003e Hardware",
    "content": "Úvod Tento článek podpory popisuje, jak můžete používat spouštěcí monitor FlightScope se Swing Catalyst. Swing Catalyst bude integrovat a ukládat všechna data FlightScope při nahrávání nového pokusu. Aby bylo možné integraci povolit, musí být software FlightScope spuštěn ve stejné době jako Swing Catalyst.\nVztahuje se na Uživatelé se spouštěcím monitorem FlightScope. Podporované modely: Řady X1, X2, X2 elite a X3.\nŘady Xi a Xi+.\nInstalace Aby Swing Catalyst rozpoznal a přečetl údaje o úderu z FlightScope, je nutné povolit režim serveru v softwaru FlightScope.\nSpusťte FlightScope a klikněte na tlačítko “Rozšířená nastavení” v hlavní nabídce. (V novějších verzích FlightScope můžete stisknout klávesu ALT na klávesnici, aby se zobrazila nabídka). Click the Advanced Settings button, located bottom right and a menu bar will show on the top of the screen. Click Networking, and select Server from the list. Verify that “Server Port” is set to 1248 and press Ok.\nNote: The server name and server IP address may vary depending on if you’re connected via USB X2 (Ethernet for X2 Elite) and or WiFi. It should not be necessary to change this.\nGo to Player Comparison or similar mode in FlightScope. Make sure FlightScope is tracking and displaying shots.\nStart Swing Catalyst and keep FlightScope running in the background.\nGo to the Swing Catalyst Main Menu - Settings - Hardware and tick off “Enabled” under Launch Monitor.\nIf it says disconnected, make sure the FlightScope application is running and that the FlightScope unit is connected to the PC or WiFi network.\nFlightScope should say, Server active, 1 clients. This means Swing Catalyst successfully has connected to the FlightScope.\nKnown Issues FlightScope is not shown as connected, even if FlightScope software is running and tracking shots and server mode is enabled.\nTry restarting FlightScope and Swing Catalyst. Start FlightScope first.\nTry setting server mode to None, then turn it back on again. See step 3.\nFlightScope is displayed on the wrong screen.\nTo move FlightScope to another screen: Click on the FlightScope program, and move the mouse cursor to the other monitor. While leaving the mouse cursor on the desired screen, click the F11 button. FlightScope should now be running on the other screen.\nLast updated: 2021-06-16 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Tento článek podpory popisuje, jak můžete používat spouštěcí monitor FlightScope se Swing Catalyst. Swing Catalyst bude integrovat a ukládat všechny...",
    "tags": [
      "Usb-Camera",
      "Launch-Monitor"
    ],
    "title": "Jak používat FlightScope se Swing Catalyst",
    "uri": "/sc-support/cs/hardware/flightscope-setup/index.html"
